; Microphone clock and capture for the SPH0641LU4H-1.
; Why it looks like this: docs/phase0/PHASE0_HARDWARE_DESIGN_REVIEW.md, sections 3.4 and 5.
;
; One state machine, two instructions per clock period. The clock divider is the length
; of half a period in system clock cycles, so the clock is 50 % by construction.
;
; The data line is read at BOTH edges. An input passes through a two-stage synchroniser,
; so each read shows the line two system clock cycles before the edge: the end of the
; half that is just finishing. Which of the two reads carries the data depends on the
; microphone's SELECT pin, and the firmware core works that out from the samples.
;
; NOT TESTED ON HARDWARE.

.program mic_capture
.side_set 1

.wrap_target
    in pins, 1   side 1   ; clock rises.  "L": the line at the end of the low half
    in pins, 1   side 0   ; clock falls.  "H": the line at the end of the high half
.wrap
